{"title":"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A right rectangular prism whose surface area and volume are numerically equal has edge lengths <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b57dd6588620027417f2f364a7fa902d124cf21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}x, \\log_{3}x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"104\" height=\"19\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/9/4995c0a33130c7f3e72bc03e76b750bf35283c5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{4}x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"51\" height=\"19\" /> What is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/f/dcf0e6ce51321975abd84e55dc4cee47dec1a4db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x?$\" width=\"18\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/6/47643b588e71a3f3a3a829c1ccfcd405e1b74b09.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 2\\sqrt{6} \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 6\\sqrt{6} \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 24 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 48 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 576$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"436\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The surface area of this right rectangular prism is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d77d7920a301021751e6f330911dcb49cb042803.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2(\\log_{2}x\\log_{3}x+\\log_{2}x\\log_{4}x+\\log_{3}x\\log_{4}x).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"350\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>The volume of this right rectangular prism is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/0/800f6fff24f51d32b54d4491240b400a89ea6e21.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}x\\log_{3}x\\log_{4}x.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Equating the numerical values of the surface area and the volume, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/95157179f7b267173913511a44e13ee5d319d7eb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(\\log_{2}x\\log_{3}x+\\log_{2}x\\log_{4}x+\\log_{3}x\\log_{4}x)=\\log_{2}x\\log_{3}x\\log_{4}x.\\]\" width=\"493\" height=\"18\" />\nDividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b4515fb3f73bf83a433b395dfac975bfb7f05a3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{2}x\\log_{3}x\\log_{4}x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"146\" height=\"19\" /> we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/2/9a2083b1e94d1b4863154f9646d5246d1526f9fa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\left(\\frac{1}{\\log_{4}x}+\\frac{1}{\\log_{3}x}+\\frac{1}{\\log_{2}x}\\right)=1. \\hspace{15mm} (\\bigstar)\\]\" width=\"366\" height=\"43\" />\nRecall that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/6/576f27d87366f522fcbd007ed3b2c5b5e38e4df2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{b}a=\\frac{1}{\\log_{a}b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"111\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/3/0231614128752621d4d3a1e476646de5f02b7c6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{b}\\left(a^n\\right)=n\\log_{b}a,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"154\" height=\"20\" /> so we rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> as \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/8/c2806785065c7b926fbabbc2d97c96378b2006ee.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2(\\log_{x}4+\\log_{x}3+\\log_{x}2)&amp;=1 \\\\ 2\\log_{x}24&amp;=1 \\\\ \\log_{x}576&amp;=1 \\\\ x&amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(E)}\\ 576}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"298\" height=\"104\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We know that the formulae for the surface area and volume of a right rectangular prism are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/e/7ce969745009bf66404b0a6e98a0cbb20b1c95e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S=2lw+2wh+2lh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"170\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/c/eec6996c0c94d0ef7194170a62d5c4de80dc3bb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$V=lwh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" />, respectively.\nIt is given that these values are numerically equal, so we can set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/3/1131a7c9bbcef72a353a4af1b1b0f9d0cdcf415a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2lw+2wh+2lh=lwh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"187\" height=\"16\" />.\nDividing both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/8/b380dddeaebadb5af356c7d76667d031775700dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$lwh$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/5880d3cfe563dfce6d4f7ee3d60fe7ec00787ab3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{h} + \\frac{2}{l} + \\frac{2}{w} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"125\" height=\"38\" />.\nWe then substitute values for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/e/9ee4b825a2e36ae093ed7be5e4851ef453b34914.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/8/8189a5b5a0917b8c93350827be4038af1839139d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, which yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/1/831c86c7781d3d42a2d5c0aa63c0b6fd40f3b0a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2}{\\log_2 x} + \\frac{2}{\\log_3 x} + \\frac{2}{\\log_4 x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"191\" height=\"43\" />.\nThen, we can recall the logarithm base-change formula <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/8/6e80680ac271670c4b0869b197cb2afc37220da5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_b a = \\frac{\\log_x a}{\\log_x b}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"117\" height=\"44\" />. \nWe can use this formula to change all the sidelengths to log base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/8/51805fb2194403a40710f8047bac739d3fa6307c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_3 x = \\frac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 3}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/4/e943036cb30109438a43caf7b72a17276b96a749.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\log_4 x = \\frac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 4}\\]\" width=\"114\" height=\"42\" />\nThen substitute back into our equation to get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060e8eba7372ea11aab12781334f5c95b8f3b78a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = \\frac{2}{\\log_2 x} + \\frac{2}{\\dfrac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 3}} + \\frac{2}{\\dfrac{\\log_2 x}{\\log_2 4}}\\]\" width=\"227\" height=\"64\" />.\nSimplifying this equation, as well as the fact that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c87242f9f18822ec5b0357d1f5af6619827cc3ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_2 4 = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"78\" height=\"19\" />, we get:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf37c1b1aba79f40011a00de473d1e4361db29fe.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1 = \\frac{2}{\\log_2 x} + \\frac{2\\log_2 3}{\\log_2 x} + \\frac{4}{\\log_2 x}\\]\" width=\"230\" height=\"42\" />\nFurther simplification yields:\n\\begin{align*}\n1 &amp;= \\frac{2+2\\log_2 3+4}{\\log_2 x} \\\\\n1 &amp;= \\frac{6+\\log_2 9}{\\log_2 x} \\\\\n\\log_2 x &amp;= 6+\\log_2 9 \\\\\n\\log_2 x - \\log_2 9 &amp;= 6 \\\\\n\\log_2 \\frac{x}{9} &amp;= 6 \\\\\n\\frac{x}{9} &amp;= 2^6 \\\\\nx &amp;= 9 \\cdot 64 = \\boxed{\\text{(E) } 576}\n\\end{align*}\n</p><p>~CrazyHydra\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wlDlByKI7A8?t=649\">https://youtu.be/wlDlByKI7A8?t=649</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A\">2021 Fall AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_16\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_17\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_23\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_Fall_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_25\" title=\"2021 Fall AMC 12A Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"2\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_12_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 12 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 12 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017153556\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.036 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.053 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 245/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2446/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 306/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5872/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.738      1 -total\n 55.47%    7.621      1 Template:AMC12_box\n 42.92%    5.897      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:22231:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017153556 and revision id 291747. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}